# Equinox Design System

Equinox is a native **macOS menu-bar calendar app** (SwiftUI + AppKit, no web layer). Its design language is precise, restrained, and native-macOS: a celestial mark, glass panels floating over the desktop, adaptive system surfaces, and **one** deliberate brand-blue accent.

**Source of truth is the code, not this file.** Read these before styling anything:

| What | Where |
|------|-------|
| Every token — spacing, radii, colors, fonts, opacities, shadows | `equinox/UI/Design/DesignTokens.swift` |
| S/M/L sizing (cell, panel, sheet, toolbar) | `equinox/UI/Design/SizeMetrics.swift` |
| Buttons, cards, badges, chips, banners, join CTA | `equinox/UI/Design/EquinoxComponents.swift` |
| Panel chrome, glass, toolbar buttons | `equinox/UI/Design/PanelComponents.swift` |
| Settings sections, rows, pickers, footers | `equinox/UI/Design/SettingsComponents.swift` |
| Sheets, error banners, confirm dialogs | `equinox/UI/Design/ModalComponents.swift` |
| Accessibility labels & helpers | `equinox/UI/Design/AccessibilityHelpers.swift` |

`equinoxTests/DesignSystemComplianceTests.swift` enforces much of this — it fails the build on raw `Color.primary.opacity(…)`, `.font(.system(size:))`, bare `.white`/`.black`, magic `.opacity(0.…)` literals outside `Design/`, and on more than one `.glassEffect(`. Add a token instead of a literal.

The values below document intent. Where they disagree with the Swift files, the Swift files win.

---

## Color (light · dark)

**Accent — exactly one.** `AccentColor` `#3373F2` · `#598CFF`. Carries today's circle, selection ring, primary buttons, the join CTA, relative-time cues. Hover → `AccentStrong` `#1F5FE0` · `#6F9BFF`. Selection fill `accentSoft` (accent @16%); selected outline `accentRing` (accent @55%). Never introduce a second brand color.

**Surfaces are adaptive system colors, not fixed hex.** `ColorToken.surfacePrimary`/`surfaceWindow` → `.windowBackgroundColor`, `surfaceSecondary` → `.controlBackgroundColor`, `surfaceRaised` (fields) → `.textBackgroundColor`. They track the system appearance for free — do not replace them with literals or asset colors.

Asset colors exist only where AppKit has no equivalent: `WeekendTint` `#DBE0EB` · `#424752`, `MonthBoundary` `#808C99` · `#99A6B2`.

**Ink.** Use `Color.primary` / `.secondary` and the `StateOpacity` tokens on top — never `rgba` equivalents or bare `.white`/`.black` (the menu-bar renderer is the one exception, via `MenuBarDesign.previewInk*`/`templateInk`).

**Hairlines & fills** (primary-ink opacities, all in `ColorToken`): `hairlineBorder` 6%, `separator` 10%, `interactionSubtle` 4% → `interactionRest` 6% → `interactionHover` 8% → `interactionPress` 10%.

**Semantic = Apple system.** `SemanticRed` `#FF3B30`·`#FF453A`, `SemanticOrange` `#FF9500`·`#FF9F0A`, `SemanticGreen` `#34C759`·`#30D158`, `SemanticBlue` `#007AFF`·`#0A84FF`; aliased as `warning`/`success`/`error`. Per-calendar event dots come from EventKit calendar colors via `DayEventColors`. **RSVP:** accepted→green, tentative→orange, declined→red (`ParticipationChipStyle`).

