## Typography — Apple system faces

SF Pro for UI, **SF Pro Rounded** for day numerals (`dayNumeralFont`), **SF Mono** for times and week numbers (`monoTimeFont`). All via system font APIs — no font files ship.

Sizes are not hard-coded at call sites: base size comes from `SizeMetrics.fontSize` (S 11 · M 13 · L 15) and the helpers derive from it — `calendarTitleFont`, `agendaSectionTitleFont` (+1), `agendaSectionSubtitleFont` (−1), `microFont` (7), `weekdayHeaderFont` (caption2 semibold), `panelIconFont`, `emptyStateIconFont`, `aboutTitleFont`. Uppercase weekday headers get `weekdayHeaderTracking` (4% of font size).

Reach for a semantic style (`.headline`, `.caption`) or one of these helpers. Never `.font(.system(size:))` in a feature view — the compliance test rejects it.

